==Strategy==
Due to the difficulty of this stage, it is recommended to just use a [[Shop Items|Treasure Radar]] on the [[Master of the Fist (Veteran)|first stage]] for most players who just want [[Akuma Giraffe (Rare Cat)|Akuma Giraffe]].

The boss of the stage, [[Akuma (Enemy)|Akuma]], is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemy]] with massive range, fast attacks, some piercing range that allows him to push harder and high health, making him a tough opponent to beat. This combination of factors make most units unusable against him. The main notable exceptions are rusher units, notably [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], who can get into his range between attacks and take away a good chunk of Akuma's health. Tanks such as [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]], [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]], or, if possible, [[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Doktor Heaven]] in her Normal Form can also do a good job stalling and chipping away at the boss's health. Additionally, [[Musashi Miyamoto (Legend Rare Cat)|Musashi Miyamoto]], if you are lucky enough to have him, can tank a lot of Akuma's hits and has ridiculously high anti-Dark DPS, meaning that two or three of him can make short work of Akuma.

Although extremely difficult to do properly, you could freeze Akuma and pray he stays frozen using [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]. Freeze Up and Speed Up Combos are mandatory for players without good timing, so bring enough along for Bombercat to perma-freeze the boss. Once a Bombercat is getting close to Akuma, use the Thunderbolt Cannon to freeze it, so Bomber has a chance to get in. It would be ideal if Akuma was by his base, so he won't get knocked out of Bomber's range when reached by the attackers tasked with killing him. Alternatively, this can be done with [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]], but be aware that he is not reliable here due to his cost of 4,500¢ and low uptime, further worsened by the more reliable domination of Bombercat and the rate at which the enemies push here. [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Nobunaga]], if timed well, can make this stage trivial, being able to permafreeze Akuma and having high enough HP to tank a hit. If freezing does not work, using Cats that dodge Dark enemies can help hold back the enemies, such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)#Talents|Flying Ninja Cat]].

[[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|The Nekolugas]] are great cats to use here, as most of them have enough range to outrange Akuma and they can either CC or deal a good chunk of damage to Akuma over time.

